# Legacy fallback

This project uses Cursor's modern rules format: see `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.
If your Cursor version doesn't pick those up automatically, read them in this order
before starting any task:

1. .cursor/rules/00-global.mdc   (always applies — production-grade code, no
   hardcoding, mandatory test coverage)
2. .cursor/rules/10-backend-go.mdc
3. .cursor/rules/20-frontend-web.mdc
4. .cursor/rules/30-database.mdc
5. .cursor/rules/40-testing.mdc

Then read the spec, in order, before writing any code:

1. spec/00-overview.md
2. spec/01-schema.md
3. spec/02-build-order.md
4. spec/03-ecommerce-integration-deferred.md (build last — not part of this pass)
